              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for supplies, then the Kannada for a telephone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಗದ್ದಲ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಗದ್ದಲ — gaddala — \"a din; a commotion\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮಾರುಕಟ್ಟೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ತುಂಬಾ ಗದ್ದಲ ಇತ್ತು. mārukaṭṭeyalli tumbā gaddala ittu. There was a lot of noise in the market."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Many voices at once; ಗಲಾಟೆ is a near twin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಗದ್ದಲ (gaddala) is usually traced to the native family of gadaṟu, gaddisu, \"to make a loud sound, to roar, to shout\" (DEDR 1189)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
