        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಜಮಾಯಿಸು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಜಮಾಯಿಸು — jamāyisu — \"to gather; to assemble\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಪಘಾತದ ನಂತರ ರಸ್ತೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಜನ ಜಮಾಯಿಸಿದರು. apaghātada nantara rasteyalli jana jamāyisidaru. After the accident people gathered on the road."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಜಮಾಯಿಸಿದೆ, jamāyiside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said of a crowd that forms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಜಮಾಯಿಸು (jamāyisu) is usually traced to an Arabic word for gathering, through Hindustani jamā, \"gathered, collected\", with the Kannada verb ending -isu. ಜಮಾ ಮಾಡು, to deposit, comes from the same word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
