          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಜಗ್ಗು — jaggu — \"to tug; to pull hard\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಗುಂಪಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಮಗು ನನ್ನ ಕೈ ಜಗ್ಗಿತು. gumpinalli magu nanna kai jaggitu. In the crowd the child tugged at my hand."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಜಗ್ಗಿದೆ, jaggide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also to sag under weight: ಹಗ್ಗ ಜಗ್ಗಿತು."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಜಗ್ಗು (jaggu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 2360 lists Kannada jaggu, \"to bend down, to sink under a weight\", in the family of sari, \"to slide\". How the sense of tugging grew from it is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
